  "description": "TURLAX crystallizes in the rhombohedral crystal system with space group R 3. Reported CIF formula moiety: C84 H67 Ce6 N3 O41,5(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Ce1 (Ce) has 8 O neighbors; Ce2 (Ce) has 9 O neighbors; Ce3 (Ce) has 8 O neighbors; Ce4 (Ce) has 9 O neighbors; Ce5 (Ce) has 8 O neighbors; Ce6 (Ce) has 9 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 12 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.731-3.804 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 100.73-117.78°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C84H67Ce6N3O41·5H2O.",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
